(* DN.DEF - reconstructed 2026-08-18.

   Included immediately after STDEFINE.INC by the units that make up the DN
   program proper (as opposed to the library units):

       DN.PAS  DNUTIL.PAS  FILECOPY.PAS  FILESCOL.PAS
       FLPANELX.PAS  GAUGES.PAS  PHONES.PAS  TREE.PAS

   Its job is to mark "this translation unit is part of the DN executable".
   The symbol DN is tested 63 times across the tree - more than any other -
   and STDEFINE.INC keys the CL_MASTER decision off it (Modem + DN =>
   CL_MASTER; see the derivation block there).

   DNPRG is the companion marker used by the same family of forks to mean
   "building the program, not a plugin".

   NOTE: this is a RECONSTRUCTION. The original file was absent from the
   repository. It is defines-only, so its effect is fully visible in the
   conditional compilation below; nothing here is guesswork about code.

   This comment deliberately uses paren-star delimiters: quoted brace
   directives inside a brace comment would terminate it at their first
   close-brace and leak the remainder into live code - which is exactly
   the defect this file shipped with for a few hours. Do not write a
   literal close delimiter inside either comment style; neither nests. *)

{$DEFINE DN}
{$DEFINE DNPRG}
